{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "את קרבנו", :translit "et korbano", :gloss "the offering of him"} {:he "את", :translit "et", :gloss "[particle marking definite direct object]"} {:he "רבוי", :translit "ribbui", :gloss "inclusion / extension"} {:he "שיביא קרבן שמן וגדול", :translit "she-yavi korban shemen u-gadol", :gloss "that he bring an offering of oil and greatness"} {:he "שלחן רבו ריקם", :translit "shulchan rabbo rekam", :gloss "the table of his master empty"} {:he "שעיר עזים זכר", :translit "sa'ir izim zachar", :gloss "a male goat"} {:he "שעירת עזים נקבה", :translit "sa'irat izim nekevah", :gloss "a female goat"} {:he "עז", :translit "ez", :gloss "goat"} {:he "זכר", :translit "zachar", :gloss "male"} {:he "נקבה", :translit "nekevah", :gloss "female"} {:he "כבש", :translit "keves", :gloss "male lamb"} {:he "כבשה", :translit "kivsah", :gloss "ewe / female lamb"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Ribbui of את in the ruler's section expands the offering requirement."} {:kind :other, :note "Lexical observation: עז is common to both genders so gender must be stated separately; כבש/כבשה differ morphologically by gender."}], :frame {:text "The principle that the particle את functions as a ribbui, extending the scope of a commandment, is established in rabbinic hermeneutics (Shabbat 64a). The king's daily lavish meals are described in rabbinic sources (Berakhot 57b; Sanhedrin 20b). The morphological distinction between כבש and כבשה is noted by the Talmud (Keritot 28a), which observes that certain animal names inherently distinguish gender while others do not.", :sources ["Shabbat 64a" "Berakhot 57b" "Sanhedrin 20b" "Keritot 28a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Ribbui of את in the ruler's section expands the offering requirement.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Lexical observation: עז is common to both genders so gender must be stated separately; כבש/כבשה differ morphologically by gender.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:03.529929162Z", :model "glm-5.2"}